  "identifier": "3d-slicer",
  "name": "3D Slicer",
  "description": "Free, open-source platform for medical image informatics, image processing, and three-dimensional visualisation. Supports segmentation, registration, image-guided therapy, tractography, and 3D printing workflows across CT, MRI, PET, and ultrasound modalities. Extensible via 200+ community modules. Backed by NIH and the National Alliance for Medical Image Computing (NA-MIC), maintained by Brigham and Women's Hospital and Kitware.",
