  "mach:judgement": "Adopt",
  "mach:judgementReason": "The definitive open-source platform for medical image computing. 2,452 GitHub stars, 20+ years of NIH-funded development, and a global community of 200+ extension modules covering segmentation, registration, tractography, and image-guided therapy. Runs on Linux, macOS, and Windows; extensible in Python. Used across academic medical centres, research hospitals, and clinical trials worldwide. BSD-style licence with no commercial restrictions. The default choice for any team building medical image analysis workflows that need an extensible, well-documented, and clinically proven platform.",
